#: includes/class-ai-settings.php:186
msgid "Scan the content of posts and pages for AI images."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-settings.php:190
msgid "Enable this if some images inside your posts or pages are not being detected by AI Transparency. When enabled, the plugin scans the HTML content and looks for images that may need an AI disclosure."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-settings.php:199
msgid "Match images by URL"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-settings.php:205
msgid "Try to identify images by their URL."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-settings.php:209
msgid "Enable this when your theme or another plugin creates image tags without the usual WordPress attachment ID. AI Transparency will try to find the corresponding Media Library item using the image URL. This is particularly useful for custom image tags and lazy-loaded images."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-settings.php:218
msgid "Process the final HTML output"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-settings.php:224
msgid "Scan the complete page before it is sent to visitors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-settings.php:228
msgid "Enable this only if AI Transparency cannot detect some images using the other methods. The plugin scans the complete HTML generated by WordPress, the theme and other plugins. This uses PHP output buffering and may require additional server resources."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-settings.php:244
msgid "These options control how AI Transparency searches for images that may require an AI disclosure. All options are disabled by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-settings.php:251
msgid "You normally do not need to enable these options unless some AI-classified images are not being detected on your website. Start with the least invasive option and only enable the final HTML scan if necessary."
msgstr ""
